Why Use a Nonce?
A nonce (number used once) is a random value generated per request to ensure uniqueness and freshness.

🔐 Benefits:
Prevents replay attacks: If an attacker captures the signed payload and resends it later, the server will reject it if the nonce has already been used.

Ensures message uniqueness: Even if the same code is selected twice, the payload will differ because the nonce is different.

Pairs well with expiry: If the attacker uses it quickly, the timestamp adds another protection.

📦 What Will Be Signed?
The mobile app will sign this structure (as a string):

plaintext
Copy
Edit
challengeId:selectedCode:expiresAt:nonce
The backend will:

Retrieve challenge details (by challengeId).

Check if nonce matches the one stored.

Check if timestamp is not expired.

Verify the digital signature.

